# KORTEX OS — Docker environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `docker/.env` and fill in real values. `docker/.env` is
# already git-ignored (repo-root .gitignore: `.env` / `.env.*` / `!.env.example`)
# -- never commit it. This file must never contain a real secret value.
#
# See implementation_plan.md §5 (Key/Secret Management) for the full
# evidence behind every variable below.

# --- Required secrets --------------------------------------------------------
# 32-byte key material, either a "0x"-prefixed 64-hex-character string or a
# UTF-8 value of at least 32 bytes. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# These are the SAME two environment variables kernel_bootstrap.py already
# reads (kernel_bootstrap.py:_resolve_key) -- no new key-management
# subsystem is introduced. If either is left unset, this image's entrypoint
# refuses to start (docker/entrypoint.sh) rather than silently falling back
# to an ephemeral, non-persistent key.
#
# Nothing in the current architecture persists these across container
# replacement -- you (the operator) must supply the SAME values again on
# every redeploy, via your own secrets manager/vault/orchestrator. This is
# the standard containerized-application pattern; it is not a KORTEX-Docker-
# specific gap and is documented, not hidden (implementation_plan.md §5, §20 OD-2).
# NOTE: these placeholders are deliberately NOT a validly-formatted key --
# entrypoint.sh's preflight will refuse to start until you replace them with
# real generated values, so a careless `cp .env.example .env` without
# editing it cannot silently run with weak/predictable key material.
KORTEX_MASTER_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF__openssl_rand_-hex_32
KORTEX_AUTH_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF__openssl_rand_-hex_32

# --- Optional secrets ---------------------------------------------------------
# Falls back to KORTEX_MASTER_KEY if unset (backup/crypto.py's own existing
# fallback order -- fails closed if neither resolves).
# KORTEX_BACKUP_KEY=

# --- Storage/database (already defaulted correctly by the image itself;
#     shown here for visibility -- override only if you know what you are
#     changing, e.g. a different volume mount point) --------------------------
# KORTEX_STORAGE_DIR=storage_data
# KORTEX_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:////data/storage_data/kortex_local.db
